# Code owners for the ARPA-H fork of the Copenhagen theme.
#
# Two things about CODEOWNERS that make this file easy to get wrong:
#
#   1. Owners must have WRITE access to this repository. A user or team with
#      only read access is treated as unresolvable.
#   2. GitHub SILENTLY IGNORES any rule whose owner it cannot resolve. There
#      is no warning on the PR and no failing check - the paths simply end up
#      with no owner, and a `require_code_owner_review` branch rule covering
#      them is then vacuously satisfied.
#
# Because of (2) a stale owner disables the review requirement instead of
# breaking loudly, which is exactly what happened here: this file still
# carried the upstream zendesk/copenhagen_theme rules (@zendesk/vikings,
# @zendesk/localization, @zendesk/butlers). Those teams do not exist in the
# ARPA-H organization, so every rule resolved to "Unknown owner" and the
# `require_code_owner_review` rule on `main` enforced nothing.
#
# The "Validate CODEOWNERS" workflow (.github/workflows/codeowners.yml) now
# fails the build whenever this file has resolution errors, so the fail-open
# cannot recur unnoticed.

